  "verdict": [
    "The model earns its place, but on 1 of 3 typologies only: ACCOUNT_TAKEOVER. Everywhere else the rules alone match the full system inside the measurement error, so the architecture is justified by those 1 rather than by all 3.",
    "Our model ALONE (0.415) scores below a single raw feature (0.457) and below the rules alone (0.875). The model is only useful in combination; it must never be described as the system's engine."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The card-testing rule gates on instrument == CARD; the offline evaluation approximates that gate from the decline signature, so this measures the architecture rather than replaying the live path exactly.",
    "Rule list membership (sanctioned, known mule, allowlist) is empty offline, so the two OVERRIDE rules and one SUPPRESS rule contribute nothing here. In production they would.",
    "47 to 57 incidents per typology. Wilson intervals are roughly 0.17 wide, so any two arms within about 0.10 of each other are not distinguishable on this corpus."
  ]
